{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1305794-should-every-db-be-a-sorcerer","id":1305794,"title":"Should every DB be a sorcerer?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-18T13:09:59-07:00","id":1305794,"title":"Should every DB be a sorcerer?","content":"After reading the DB 3e book, I have come to the conclusion that every beginning DB should probably think about becoming a sorcerer for three reasons. First, a beginning DB sorcerer gains a lot of additional functionality (the ability to use shaping rituals, the ability to use sorcerous workings, access to a control spell, and access to proprietary merits) for the low price of 1 Charm and 3 Ability dots. Second, while beginning DBs have less powerful Charms than beginning Solars, their beginning spells are just as powerful, so Sorcery ends up helping to balance the scales, especially since their extra dot of Essence improves the spells. Third, the rule of cool, as there is nothing cooler than being a spell-slinger equipped with powered combat armor while dual-wielding flame pistols. <br /> <br /> What do you think? Should every beginning DB be a dabbler in Sorcery? Would it be wrong to have every DB dabbling in Sorcery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","name":"The Fool of Creation","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T13:19:42-07:00","id":1305796,"title":"","content":"Actually, the buy-in cost for DBs is higher than it is for Solars or Lunars: DBs must first buy four Occult Charms (Excellency included) before they are allowed to take their Terrestrial Circle Sorcery Charm. This isn't a huge hurdle, but it does mean that unlike Solars, they can't really &quot;dip&quot; Sorcery and have to actually invest a good deal in occult expertise. It doesn't make Sorcery a bad option at all, it just makes it less able to be a &quot;oh and also I do Sorcery&quot; like Solars can.<br /> <br /> Lunars have a lesser barrier to entry in that they just have to take four Mental Attribute Charms (Excellencies not included), which is a <i>far</i> looser requirement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T13:38:05-07:00","id":1305800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Fool of Creation</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1305794-should-every-db-be-a-sorcerer#post1305794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading the DB 3e book, I have come to the conclusion that every beginning DB should probably think about becoming a sorcerer for three reasons. First, a beginning DB sorcerer gains a lot of additional functionality (the ability to use shaping rituals, the ability to use sorcerous workings, access to a control spell, and access to proprietary merits) for the low price of 1 Charm and 3 Ability dots. Second, while beginning DBs have less powerful Charms than beginning Solars, their beginning spells are just as powerful, so Sorcery ends up helping to balance the scales, especially since their extra dot of Essence improves the spells. Third, the rule of cool, as there is nothing cooler than being a spell-slinger equipped with powered combat armor while dual-wielding flame pistols.<br /> <br /> What do you think? Should every beginning DB be a dabbler in Sorcery? Would it be wrong to have every DB dabbling in Sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It would be terrible for the setting if that's what you mean. But thankfully in-setting characters don't make decisions based on how accessible an option is for a player (if it was, every person in Creation would be Exalted). The forms of Initiation means Sorcery isn't just something an in-setting character can just opt to dabble in.<br /> <br /> But if you want your characters to always be lucky enough to have gained access to Sorcery, sure no problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T13:45:15-07:00","id":1305802,"title":"","content":"Evocations on jade artifacts also level the playing field and are far more accessible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T14:23:25-07:00","id":1305807,"title":"","content":"Nobody dabbles in sorcery. Your initiations and/or control spell exert an effect on you that hangs around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T14:28:18-07:00","id":1305809,"title":"","content":"Are they actually more accessible for Exalted? What are the restrictions around developing sorcery as an Exalted? Of course, I have a witch for every market village, so mortal sorcerers are uncommon rather than rare, so I may be more liberal concerning sorcery than the majority of the community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","name":"The Fool of Creation","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T14:35:38-07:00","id":1305810,"title":"","content":"Well, I mean percentage wise there are most likely more sorcerers per exalt than per mortal, but it's not something <i>everyone</i> can do.<br /> <br /> If a Player decides their character is going to become a sorcerer then they are one of the ones who can learn it, of course. I suppose the assumption is that a decent chunk of the ones who don't couldn't manage in-universe if they tried. That's true for most things on the character sheet really. Your character is bad at whatever abilities you choose not to take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T14:45:10-07:00","id":1305811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Fool of Creation</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1305794-should-every-db-be-a-sorcerer?p=1305809#post1305809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they actually more accessible for Exalted? What are the restrictions around developing sorcery as an Exalted? Of course, I have a witch for every market village, so mortal sorcerers are uncommon rather than rare, so I may be more liberal concerning sorcery than the majority of the community.</div> </div> </div> </div>The village witch is why thaumaturgy exists in the game. Now if you\u2019re altering the setting that\u2019s fine, but it is an alternate setting then.<br /> <br /> Sorcery requires an initiation in-setting. It\u2019s not just an in character decision to learn a Charm - that\u2019s just how it\u2019s mechanized for players. Being one of the few students who attends the Heptagram (or equivalent institution) is a suitable initiation - but failing that a DB would need to go out and seek Mara, an Ifrit, drug themselves with alchemy for years, etc etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T16:06:34-07:00","id":1305837,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that, in-character, the aptitude for sorcery not being universal is a thing that applies even to at least the Terrestrial Exalted. It is stated in What Fire Has Wrought that not everybody who graduates from the Heptagram comes away with initiation into sorcery; even if their talents and inclinations are sufficient to be accepted to that institute, some Exalted just lack the correct qualities to break through into that access to power.<br /> <br /> That's just a matter of characterizing the setting, though. Really, what arguments there are against sorcery for every character in a play group are somewhat loose; there are opportunity costs sure, but I'd say none so high that one might feel a significant strain for including at least a starting package for sorcery. I know of at least one person who reports that their whole Dragon Blooded play group had the characters as sorcerers.<br /> <br /> So it really does come down to a question of whether or not one views their character concept as a sorcerer in particular. If it doesn't, I think that's liable to take priority over the utilitarian advantages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T16:28:44-07:00","id":1305843,"title":"","content":"This isn't the question to be asking. The question to be asking is how cool it is for the PCs or the villains to show up as an elite force of ivory tower wizards that can incinerate buildings and call forth storms.<br /> <br /> More seriously though, on balance it's extremely effective for everyone of any type of exalt to just be a sorcerer, but it isn't so great that you need to do it. Also there's so many things that offer stuff like that, like should every DB have an heirloom weapon like out of the book? Probably. They give really good bonuses to the bloodline. It's not so crazy that anyone should be sacrificing their character concept to do it though. Not to mention I find most Exalts of any description to be more than up to the challenges they face either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T16:34:58-07:00","id":1305845,"title":"","content":"Any character can be a sorcerer. But you can\u2019t just BE a sorcerer.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s not just a matter of The Price Of Sorcery. Every initiation has fringe benefits and unique connections to play off. Kinda the whole point of imitation merits and control spells is so that having sorcery is enough to give any character a pretty complete flavour/aesthetic/concept.<br /> <br /> None of those concepts are \u201cDragon blooded who dipped into the sorcery shop because why not, eh?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Or... I mean I guess A couple of them are a bit like that but with better words and unique elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T01:48:23-07:00","id":1305932,"title":"","content":"I'm quite fond of some of those early Exalted 1e depictions of the First Age where it was stated that it tended to be the case that every Exalt knew some degree of sorcery, and sorcery as accepted as the birthright of the Exalted. I'm not so up on the idea that some Exalts have it in them to be sorcerers and others do not (for mortals that's fine, but not Exalts). So I'm not averse to the idea that the Dragonblooded could form such a culture like that. That said, it would probably clash with the Realm as currently intended for that to be the case, however, so not really suitable for the default setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T02:54:48-07:00","id":1305941,"title":"","content":"An all sorcerer dragon blooded game is actually pretty easy to justify while preserving the &quot;sorcery is rare&quot; setting conceit.<br /> <br /> &quot;We met at the heptagram&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T03:09:04-07:00","id":1305946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1305794-should-every-db-be-a-sorcerer?p=1305932#post1305932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-snip-</div> </div> </div> </div>Cooking food is the birthright of humanity. There are still people who are terrible at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T03:16:54-07:00","id":1305949,"title":"","content":"I had intended to make about the same point; not all Exalted will have the aptitude to develop just about any other skill. Why should sorcery be any different?<br /> <br /> I also find the Heptagram in particular enriched both by the idea that not every graduate leaves with sorcery and that the education is of value regardless.<br /> <br /> I might have gotten those points in first were it not for the fact that <i>my goddamn browser has stopped being able to post things here again!!!</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T03:41:21-07:00","id":1305953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Fool of Creation</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1305794-should-every-db-be-a-sorcerer?p=1305809#post1305809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they actually more accessible for Exalted? What are the restrictions around developing sorcery as an Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>More accessible in that if learning in an academic environment under controlled conditions doesn't work for them they\u2019re more likely to survive the alternatives. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T04:27:25-07:00","id":1305963,"title":"","content":"I think generally most of us can agree that it would be bad for the setting if nearly every Dragonblood has sorcery (just as if it would be bad if nearly all of them practiced Immaculate Martial Arts), but if you want all your PCs to have sorcery, sure. Not a big deal.<br /> Personally, I'd find that boring (because I think the PCs would be a bit similar), but if I was running the game and all the PCs wanted to be sorcerers... sure. Not a big deal. I'd probably encourage them to have different signature spells, aspects, favoured abilities, etc, so they weren't too samey. And initiations, but then, as Elfive said...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1305794-should-every-db-be-a-sorcerer?p=1305941#post1305941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An all sorcerer dragon blooded game is actually pretty easy to justify while preserving the &quot;sorcery is rare&quot; setting conceit.<br /> <br /> &quot;We met at the heptagram&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the easiest way, so then most of them are going to have the Heptagram initiation (though not all, I'm sure if someone wanted a different one they could justify it).<br /> <br /> I will say though...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Fool of Creation</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> First, a beginning DB sorcerer gains a lot of additional functionality (the ability to use shaping rituals, the ability to use sorcerous workings, access to a control spell, and access to proprietary merits) for the low price of</div> </div> </div> </div>5 charms (though probably you'll take a free excellency, which will be one of those)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and 3 Ability dots. Second, while beginning DBs have less powerful Charms than beginning Solars, their beginning spells are just as powerful, so Sorcery ends up helping to balance the scales, especially since their extra dot of Essence improves the spells. </div> </div> </div>So, while there's the point about actually needing 5 occult charms to get 1 spell and access to workings, it's still pretty strong. As you said, their spells are just as powerful as a starting Solar's (their Occult excellency is a bit worse, but their Essence is better).<br /> So I'd agree that <b>Sorcery is a very strong choice for a Dragonblood.</b><br /> <br /> On the other hand:<br /> <b>Immaculate Martial Arts are a very strong choice for a Dragonblood.</b> They're martial arts that let you wear armour, and for a Dragonblood are kind of Solar Tier. (It's difficult to compare, but with Aura they're probably close to a style with Mastery.)<br /> And there are <i>no prerequisites beyond a combat ability, </i>which obviously you probably want anyway.<br /> They don't even cost more XP than DB charms (unlike spells), and you'll be able to scale more as you go up in XP (whereas spells cap out at Essence 1, though there is a good Essence 3 charm DB sorcerers can get).<br /> And you can combine multiple Immaculate Styles, whereas spells don't tend to combo very well (a little; Wood Dragon Claw works with Brawl, etc. But there's not much in the way of combat charms you can use to boost Death of Obsidian Butterflies).<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations are a very strong choice for a Dragonblood. </b>Your extra merits means you can easily start with an artefact weapon (or armour). You're Resonant with Jade, which means you can get Mastery effects on Jade weapons, same as a Solar. You have to pay slightly more XP than a Solar would, but you do get to buy Essence 1+2 evocations from your starting charms, you can get 2-5 evocations from a tree at character creation (when the extra XP doesn't matter).<br /> Also, Evocations combo really well with other stuff. For example, you can combo a magic bow that shoots lightning bolts with Archery charms, or a trident for fighting underwater with Melee charms.<br /> Also, a Lunar who walks around with a giant silver axe is kind of giving themselves away as a monstrous demon-beast. A Dragonblood who walks around with a huge jade spear is giving themselves away as a Demigod who you should probably pay homage to.<br /> <br /> <b>Social charms are a very strong choice for a Dragonblood. </b>A)They have a good set of social charms, though mostly focused on inspiring emotions. B)You're an aristocrat in an intrigue-laden world-spanning power. You've probably started with money and resources. It's quite likely you're in a lot more social situations than the average group of Solars.<br /> <br /> <b>Craft charms are a strong choice for Dragonblood.</b> Okay, in a mixed game you can't compete with the speed of Solar charms. But unlike Solars (and Lunars), you can probably much more easily get your hands on magic materials, which I always find is a big problem for Celestial crafters.<br /> <br /> <b>Linguistics charms are a good choice for Dragonblood.</b> Wind-Carried Words is game-changing.<br /> <br /> Etc, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, my point is, yes, sorcery is a strong choice. But so are many other options, and a starting DB with, say, 5 spells, has spent more like half their charms on being a sorcerer. Another character could have bought the Martial Arts excellency and the first four charms of Wood Dragon and Air Dragon.<br /> Or the first four evocations of a magic sword's tree and 4 melee charms.<br /> <br /> So, if you have a group of four players who are really interested in having powerful characters (as opposed to four who are more interested in fluff and don't care too much about power), then I don't think you'll get four sorcerers. Immaculate Martial Arts and evocations are too powerful a choice, and someone having plenty of social charms is always useful.<br /> (And obviously social charms aren't really comparable to spells; you can't really make a social-sorcerer whose spells are better at socialising than DB social charms.)<br /> <br /> Thus, I think it's likely, even for players who are quite interested in having powerful characters, that they'll be a sorcerer or not a sorcerer depending on their character concept.<br /> (Which is... how it ought to work. So it's good design really. I think if Sorcery didn't require four other Occult charms, it would be way too popular, but that requirement means it requires a serious investment. I suspect the Lunars' requirement for four other Mental attribute charms was inspired by it; while it's not very onerous, it does ensure that being a sorcerer is a big part of the character; your Full Moon combat monster with 14 combat charms can't go &quot;oh, I could do with the permanent soak bonus from having Invulnerable Skin of Bronze as a signature spell, I'll just pick that up with my last charm purchase, even though it's not at all a significant part of my character.&quot; Especially as there aren't so many Essence 1 mental attribute charms available that you can easily pick up four Perception charms that are purely about combat against non-spirits. An Essence 1 Lunar with four mental charms quite likely has something occulty. Of the three Lunars in the game I run with mental charms, 2 have spirit-fighting charms and the other has the Wits charm so he can stick a magical fire gem in his flesh so he can have burning fists.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fool of Creation</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">as there is nothing cooler than being a spell-slinger equipped with powered combat armor while dual-wielding flame pistols.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is absolutely a fine concept.<br /> But if you want to take a really strong choice (which is of course, not always the best way to build a character, but it was your starting point so we'll go with that), you're probably better off taking some Evocations for your flame-pistols and power-armour, and some Archery charms (like the one for reflexively reloading... although that's a common evocation), instead of four Occult charms and a few Spells.<br /> <br /> I think the sorcerer with power armour and flame-pistols is more interesting and cool, but the more powerful choice in terms of combat is Evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-19-2019, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T04:41:35-07:00","id":1305966,"title":"","content":"Missed the prerequisite during the first read through, but I think that even combat oriented character may have some utility from Occult charms. At least one DB of a group should have the ability to engage dematerialized opponents. You need Earth or Fire Style to do so otherwise as beginning characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","name":"The Fool of Creation","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T04:46:31-07:00","id":1305968,"title":"","content":"What charms in Earth and Fire let you do that?<br /> <br /> But yes, I agree, you probably do want someone in the group to take some Occult charms. Doesn't have to be everyone, but someone should.<br /> <br /> Now I'm thinking of the time where our six 200xp-ish Solars+Lunars were running around our wrecked floating ship trying to defeat one single war ghost who kept killing our crew, because not one of us had ever bought charms for interacting with dematerialised spirits.<br /> <br /> Of course, that later led to the high-xp game of DB spies where the ST insisted we all get some charms for dealing with spirits so that debacle didn't happen again... only then it turned out none of us had bought the Larceny charm for knowing if people are spying on you. Pretty important for spies.<br /> <br /> It's all trade-offs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T05:59:54-07:00","id":1305977,"title":"","content":"Of course, one of the advantages of being a sorcerer is that you can have Demons and Elementals as a force multiplier. While Blood Apes are crude, they can mess up dematerialized spirits without you having to really do anything. Elementals are effective counters to more mundane enemies, and a couple of bound greenmaws are fearsome protectors as long as you feed them meat on a regular basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","name":"The Fool of Creation","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T16:03:22-07:00","id":1306104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1305794-should-every-db-be-a-sorcerer?p=1305968#post1305968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What charms in Earth and Fire let you do that?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ghost-grounding blow and God-immolating strike.<br /> Hilariously though, neither those charms nor the styles they are in allow the user to see or touch dematerialised beings. So you still need to dip occult.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To be clear, it\u2019s not plain that this is the intention. God-immolating in particular specifies that it does more damage to dematerialised spirits while Not having a prereqs that allows them to be touched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","user":"Maseiken","date":". 04-19-2019, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T16:15:45-07:00","id":1306106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1305794-should-every-db-be-a-sorcerer?p=1305963#post1305963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the easiest way, so then most of them are going to have the Heptagram initiation (though not all, I'm sure if someone wanted a different one they could justify it).</div> </div> </div> </div>The easiest way to justify it is to simply quote the first paragraph on p.309, under the heading &quot;Student of the Heptagram&quot;:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Graduates of the Heptagram initiate into sorcery through many different paths. The following is only the most common initiation. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T16:16:24-07:00","id":1306107,"title":"","content":"This entire thread feels more about &quot;You should do what makes a character who's optimal at 'winning' the game&quot; than actually building a character. While there is more breadth of powers gained by being a sorcerer, I think the entire premise that &quot;I have more power this way, so every character should hav eit&quot; isn't at least in the spirit of things.<br /> <br /> Sometimes a character just isn't going to be interested in the stuff sorcery gains. Nothing wrong if you do, but the idea that it's &quot;optimal&quot; to build a character in such a way in a non-competitive game is kind of odd to me at times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T17:38:12-07:00","id":1306116,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the idea of people naturally optimizing themselves in-character <i>sounds</i> reasonable, but it all falls apart once I remember how many times I've eaten snack cakes this week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T18:18:00-07:00","id":1306131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1305794-should-every-db-be-a-sorcerer?p=1306116#post1306116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the idea of people naturally optimizing themselves in-character <i>sounds</i> reasonable, but it all falls apart once I remember how many times I've eaten snack cakes this week.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah like, to be the best sorcerer you can be you should really have Dodge and Brawl at 5 which is not hard at chargen.<br /> That said, \u201cwhat I spent all these years bowing a scraping and studying, finally mastered the diagrams, summoned and bound this Blood Ape into my service as a bodyguard, and now I\u2019m supposed to Sweat? Outside? So I can avoid getting hurt?<br /> <br /> That\u2019s what the demon is for, chief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T18:50:25-07:00","id":1306139,"title":"","content":"Also doesn't the Realm and Creation at large view sorcerers and sorcery as more of a necessary danger? Like pretty sure WFHW says that most people don't understand sorcery enough to trust it and the way it makes things go causes people to be uncomfortable. So I'd think a lot of them would be more reluctant on the grounds that they don't have the same authority to pick their initiation and not wanting to risk certain ones and how they effect you. Like I know a few people who wouldn't touch sorcery if they thought their best shot was mara feeding them souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T03:06:42-07:00","id":1306212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Fool of Creation</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1305794-should-every-db-be-a-sorcerer?p=1305977#post1305977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, one of the advantages of being a sorcerer is that you can have Demons and Elementals as a force multiplier. While Blood Apes are crude, they can mess up dematerialized spirits without you having to really do anything. Elementals are effective counters to more mundane enemies, and a couple of bound greenmaws are fearsome protectors as long as you feed them meat on a regular basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true, but that's not really fitting your image of a power-armoured, fire-pistol-wielding badass.<br /> <br /> And demons can be problematic, difficult to control, etc. That's why you have to get demon insurance.<br /> I mean, let's imagine your sorceress wants to get a handsome boyfriend. You meet a hot dude at a teahouse, and invite him round to your bachelorette pad, which you've had your slaves clean up, cook a nice meal, etc. But while he's there, he keeps sniffing and looking uncomfortable. There's no second date. Why? It's those damn stinky blood apes! They're the worst room-mates ever.<br /> You've got to think about these things!<br /> <br /> Elementals are generally a bit less problematic, but a)not always (Greenmaws have to be watched because they tend to eat everything), and b)they only last a month. Though that's not a huge issue unless you need to summon an army.<br /> <br /> (Also, at high XP combat spirits are basically just ways for your enemies to easily farm Initiative.)<br /> <br /> This is not say Summon Demon isn't worth 10xp. It absolutely is. I'd say it's probably one of the best Essence 1 charm picks in the game. Just that it's not as amazing as it might first appear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Like pretty sure WFHW says that most people don't understand sorcery enough to trust it and the way it makes things go causes people to be uncomfortable.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why sorcerers don't get invited to parties.<br /> As I said, this is important!<br /> <br /> Though, in previous editions, it depended on the House. Mnemon and Ledaal were generally fine with it, whereas Pelleps was incredibly prejudiced against sorcerers, and Pelleps male sorcerers would try and get married into a more accepting house.<br /> Nellens was actually very keen on sorcerers (because they hardly had any) and would try and bribe sorcerers from other houses to defect.<br /> <br /> I can't access my pdfs (damn desktop PC is on the fritz) so I don't remember what WFHW says. I think I remember the anti-sorcerer attitudes being toned down a bit, but still there. Although of course, sorcerers are even weirder in this edition than 2nd ed (but then, in 2nd ed only the weird ones were considered &quot;sorcerers&quot; anyway).<br /> I guess Ragara is probably more comfortable with sorcerers than in 2nd, with their new obsession with the Occult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T03:11:59-07:00","id":1306213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1305794-should-every-db-be-a-sorcerer?p=1306116#post1306116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the idea of people naturally optimizing themselves in-character <i>sounds</i> reasonable, but it all falls apart once I remember how many times I've eaten snack cakes this week.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, that made me laugh. Basically every week I think I should go on a diet, and yet...<br /> <br /> And don't forget all the time you spent watching TV, posting on this forum, playing games, or whatever. Why weren't you at the gym or reading textbooks, huh?<br /> You've got 16 hours awake every day. That's 16 hours of optimisation practice!<br /> <br /> And yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T03:12:43-07:00","id":1306215,"title":"","content":"Actually in 3e summon elemental lasts just as long as summoning a demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T03:29:13-07:00","id":1306219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1305794-should-every-db-be-a-sorcerer?p=1306131#post1306131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah like, to be the best sorcerer you can be you should really have Dodge and Brawl at 5 which is not hard at chargen.<br /> That said, \u201cwhat I spent all these years bowing a scraping and studying, finally mastered the diagrams, summoned and bound this Blood Ape into my service as a bodyguard, and now I\u2019m supposed to Sweat? Outside? So I can avoid getting hurt?<br /> <br /> That\u2019s what the demon is for, chief.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will say, while I see people's points about the irrelevance of optimisation, that's not the only thing.<br /> <br /> Yes, you might want Brawl and Dodge 5. But your sorcerer only needs Occult 5. And maybe Lore 5. And then you want this, and that, and this, and that...<br /> <br /> I have a Essence 5 Lunar with over 460xp. Maybe 480? I can't remember off-hand.<br /> <br /> My highest social pool is 5 dice (Charisma 3 and Presence 2). I have two Charisma charms (both Essence 1), to get the excellency. My Resolve is 3, and I can use charms to increase it to... 4 (without a stunt).<br /> <br /> Why, for a 460xp character, are my social stats so bad?<br /> Because I've invested heavily in combat, medicine, and tracking. I have like 14 perception charms, 5 poison charms, 10 martial arts charms, 3 dex combat charms, a strength charm, 7 medicine charms, etc. It adds up.<br /> <br /> Everything is trade-offs. You can probably at character gen focus on about two areas heavily. So in the OP's example, we've got a sorcerer (that's 5 charms right there just for one spell), Archer (probably 3 or 4 charms). Then you want some defence charms, say another 2 or 3.<br /> So that's a combat-sorcerer... and not much else.<br /> You've probably spent 6 merit points on artefacts (3 for armour, 3 for devil-casters), so you don't have a ton of social merits.<br /> <br /> And what about your attributes? You want a maxed-out Intelligence score so you're a powerful sorcerer (and don't get beaten up when you try summoning demons). So let's say mental primary. Let's say Perception 2, Int 5, Wits 4, so you've got a good Join Battle for combat and a good dice pool to banish demons if you fail your binding roll.<br /> <br /> Then you have Physical Secondary. Strength 2 (don't need it for flame weapons), Dex 5, Stamina 2. You're good at shooting, but your soak is actually quite poor.<br /> <br /> This leaves something like Cha 3, Manipulation 2, App 2.<br /> <br /> In social intrigue, in research, in craft, in athletics and survival... this character is not very good.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which is really how it should be. However you build your character, there's other things you're not much good at.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, actually the chances are, many sorcerers with a whole bunch of demons actually aren't that good at combat, and so probably are tempted to stay inside and send their demons out to do the work. They've put their points into mental attributes and abilities like Occult, Lore and so on, they probably want some social stats because it's very important as a Dynast, and so they may end up not that good at physical stuff.<br /> <br /> (Actually, in the DB games I played all the sorcerers either were not much good at combat, or got screwed because they were good at combat and sorcery but were constantly socially out-manouevred.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T03:29:56-07:00","id":1306220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1305794-should-every-db-be-a-sorcerer?p=1306215#post1306215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually in 3e summon elemental lasts just as long as summoning a demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't it only last a month? I don't have my books right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T03:33:37-07:00","id":1306221,"title":"","content":"Never says anything about a month. Just<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once summoned, the elemental must be bound to the<br /> sorcerer\u2019s will, as per Demon of the First Circle (p. 473),<br /> except that an elemental cannot break free\u2014if the binding<br /> fails, the elemental simply disperses back into raw Essence,<br /> and the sorcerer doesn\u2019t regain the Willpower spent on<br /> the spell. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T03:35:51-07:00","id":1306223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1305794-should-every-db-be-a-sorcerer?p=1306106#post1306106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The easiest way to justify it is to simply quote the first paragraph on p.309, under the heading &quot;Student of the Heptagram&quot;:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>..<br /> As teachers, we always say every student is different, and you have to teach them differently.<br /> <br /> I could well imagine that the occult texts method is the main one tried, but students can access other methods, like alchemy, negotiating with spirits*, building a phylactery, geomancy, etc, if they find that one doesn't work for them. There's only a handful of students at a time, so each one probably gets a very individualised teaching method.<br /> <br /> *I think though that they might avoid letting students negotiate with a demon for sorcery though. Dragonblood do have the right to command demons, but I can well imagine the teachers are wary of letting students negotiate with non-bound demons. Perhaps very trusted students.<br /> Still, I can also imagine a teacher binding a demon teacher to teach a student about the demomology under controlled circumstances.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}